{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/557987-pacting-for-body-parts","id":557987,"title":"Pacting for Body Parts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-17T00:41:30-07:00","id":557987,"title":"Pacting for Body Parts?","content":"I'm sure this has been answered elsewhere, but it came up and I'm curious about this. How does Pacting to take physical features from someone work? Obviously, taking away something like freckles makes sense - they lose them you gain them - but what about someone with a severed limb, or a distinctive hair color? Say someone lost their leg in Iraq, and you pact for that; do they gain a leg, or did they simply lose it some other way? Could you pact for someone's race, or their sex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:16:57-07:00","id":558152,"title":"","content":"Actually... that's not how it works. Its how external benefits like Resources or Allies work, but not internal features, like knowledge/skills or physical attributes. When a pact alters a person, it alters them, not giving away things. <br /> <br /> You can take away freckles, make someone's hair blond, regenerate a limb, all without having to take those things from someone, or put them somewhere. Its more like rewriting the pact is rewriting the personal history and genome so that they never developed lost a leg in combat, was born with blond hair, and just never had freckles in their life. <br /> <br /> Demons make pacts for parts of people's lives, not their physical characteristics. So, they could make a deal for defining relationships or their history, or they could strike pacts for changing a person's body, but you'd have to have details what the change you're making actually is. So, if someone wanted to strike a deal to become a man or woman, or become hispanic, white, black, whatever? That's all doable.<br /> <br /> Whenever you take part of a person's life, you absorb part of their appearance into their Cover. It mixes with all the other parts you had before to create a new look. If you want their full appearance, you'll have to claim their soul and take over the life as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:41:50-07:00","id":558164,"title":"","content":"Lets talk about that &quot;Where Does the Money Come From?&quot; sidebar for a moment. That's where the whole idea of you take something away from somewhere to give it to the pactee. When you ask for money, yes, that money comes from somewhere else. Same with Staff, or Allies. <br /> <br /> Why does it work this way? Its not because of some kind of Equivalent Exchange (TM). That is how the CtL pledges work, but DtD pacts work under a different principle. According to that sidebar, what happens when a demon makes a pact is that s/he's directly hacking into the pactee's personal file. Demons can only alter the people making the pact, not the wider world. Reality is just reshaping itself as an indirect consequence of the new changes to the pactee. Nature abhors a vacuum, and all that. <br /> <br /> Its like opening up a character sheet in a game, and altering the character at will. Add points here, change the history there. You can do anything to that individual you want. There's no balance to maintain, and you have free access to almost anything you can think of to alter that character. <br /> <br /> Here's where the whole &quot;someone loses their money so you get it&quot; comes from. The demon rewrites your history so that you're holding a winning lottery ticket. The actual winner from before the pact still has an actual winning ticket, and he still cashes it in. So, you end up effectively splitting the reward in this new, revised history. By all rights, that winner should have had double the pot. In the case of asking for, oh, lab assistants? Changing the pactee so he has social connections to &quot;lab assistants&quot; is great, but the money to fund those assistants has to come from somewhere. So, the budget gets cut in other areas, and other people get underfunded, and have to let go of their own staff to make up for it. Instead of making himself a fool in front of peers, the demon alters a pactee's history so that they were fun to hang with, and as a result of hanging out with these new friends, suddenly, other friendships never got to manifest itself.<br /> <br /> Reality may make compensation for these changes that are being made to the individual pactee, but its all incidental. Pacts only change individual variables on the pactee, not reach out and alter the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}